TYPEMASTER SUPABASE LOGIN SETUP

1. Authentication > Providers > Email should be enabled.
2. For easiest testing, you can turn off "Confirm email". For a real public site, keeping email confirmation ON is recommended.
3. Authentication > URL Configuration:
   - Site URL: set this to your final website URL, e.g. https://yourdomain.com
   - Add Redirect URL for login password reset, e.g. https://yourdomain.com/login.html
4. Never put a Supabase secret/service_role key in the website. This project uses only the publishable key.
5. Upload all files to the same folder/repository. New files:
   - auth.js
   - login.html
   - signup.html
   - reset-password.html
   - account.html

The login/signup system uses Supabase Auth. It does not require a database table for basic authentication.
